First dumb YANI: special level "Desert"

The level is similar to the Big Room in that the stairs are randomly
placed.  Monsters generated are from the classes a, d, r, s, w, M, S, or
Z.  Scattered throughout are small oases with a few trees.  In one
corner is a 10 x 10 temple with guaranteed altar, chest, and traps.  If
the YANIs Fremen or Pirate classes are added then this desert would be
an ideal mid-quest level.


Second dumb YANI: Tooth Fairy

The Tooth Fairy is a unique monster, represented as either n, A, or &.
It typically moves around like a unicorn.  If thrown a piece of ivory it
responds "The Tooth Fairy is grateful for your gift", drops some gold,
then randomly teleports elsewhere.  If instead it is attacked or thrown
non-ivory material it gets angry.  Upon a successful hit it (randomly)
steels one of your ivory items (including unihorns) or if you are
humanoid it reduces your wisdom by one ("You feel a sharp pain in your
mouth!").  The Tooth Fairy then teleports similar to a nymph attack.
The wisdom lost is reversible by the standard means.

